local throwHeight = 32.5;
local progressAtFirstBounce = .45;
local heightOfFirstBounce = 10;
local progressAtSecondBounce = .75;
local heightOfSecondBounce = 7;
local spinRate = 360

modelPitch = time * spinRate
transUp = throwHeight * progress;

if (progress < progressAtFirstBounce) then

	local normalizedProgress = progress / progressAtFirstBounce;
	transUp = transUp - ((normalizedProgress * normalizedProgress) * throwHeight);

elseif (progress < progressAtSecondBounce) then

	local normalizedProgress = (progress - progressAtFirstBounce) /
		(progressAtSecondBounce - progressAtFirstBounce);

	local curHeight = (normalizedProgress * 2) - 1;
	curHeight = (1 - (curHeight * curHeight)) * heightOfFirstBounce;

	transUp = (transUp - throwHeight) + curHeight;

else

	local normalizedProgress = (progress - progressAtSecondBounce) /
		(1.0 - progressAtSecondBounce);

	local curHeight = (normalizedProgress * 2) - 1;
	curHeight = (1 - (curHeight * curHeight)) * heightOfSecondBounce;

	transUp = (transUp - throwHeight) + curHeight;

end

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup_heroicdungeons1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reach Item Level 92 to Enter Heroic Dungeons!</h1><br/>
<p>Prepare by increasing your average item level to 92 for Heroic TBC Dungeons.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup_heroicdungeons2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Complete Call Board Quests and Manastorm!</h1><br/>
<p>Upgrade your gear through Call Board Daily Quests and running Manastorm.<br/><br/>
Call Board Caches provide gear based on your item level.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup_heroicdungeons3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Run Normal TBC Dungeons and Quests in Outland!</h1><br/>
<p>Participate in Normal TBC Dungeons using the Group Finder ("I" by default).<br/><br/>
Completing quests in Outland also helps you obtain better equipment.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\116_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Travel Faster!</h1><br/>
<p>Mounts greatly increase your movement speed! They can only be used outdoors.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\112_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<p>Seek out a Riding Trainer to receive your first Mount for free!<br/><br/>Select Start Quest and the nearest Riding Trainer will be tracked in your Quest Objectives and as a Yellow ? on the world map.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\116_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<p>You will receive a Mount in your bags after completing the Novice Rider quest at the Traveling Riding Trainer.<br/><br/>Open your Bags and use the Mount to learn it.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\231_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Slot 4 Active Manastorm Spells!</h1><br/>
<p>Your Manastorm Active Spell loadout can complement your build! There is no best setup, only the setup that matches your build and playstyle.<br/><br/>
Find a set of Manastorm Spells that complement your build and fill out all 4 slots!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\231_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Cogsley sells new spells and upgrades!</h1><br/>
<p>Cogsley sells many tools that increase your power and offer new utility to allow you to progress further into the Manastorm.<br/><br/>
Once you find a set of spells that work well for you, try to upgrade them as much as possible!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\246_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Character Customization Extends to Your Pets!</h1><br/>
<p>As a Hero who can have a pet battling at your side, you have the freedom to customize your pet’s appearance to suit your class fantasy!<br/><br/>
Using the Wardrobe, you can find and preview the appearance of various pets under the “Pet” tab in the upper menus.<br/><br/>
There are 5 different types of tameable pets in Ascension. Click your pet's category using the upper icons to view its cosmetics!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\246_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Pet Cosmetics Can be Found Throughout the World!</h1><br/>
<p>To obtain a new appearance for your pet, you’ll need to find its origin item. You can find this by tracking down the creature in the world and slaying it, or by buying it off another player with the Auction House.<br/><br/>
Every enemy that can be categorized as a pet type, has a chance to drop its pet cosmetic, which you can then loot and learn its appearance with Ctrl + Right Click!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\246_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use the Wardrobe to Find Your New Pet</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Wardrobe tab under Character Advancement to find your new pet and click Apply.<br/><br/>
This not only changes the appearance of your pet, but also its stats and abilities! Each pet has a different set of spells and style of play, so it’s up to you to find which pet is best for you!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\246_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Pet Cosmetics are Realm-Wide!</h1><br/>
<p>Pet Cosmetics are also saved under the Vanity tab in Character Advancement.<br/><br/>
If you ever lose your pet or want to use its appearance and abilities on another character, you can have it delivered through Vanity!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\4_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Save a Mystic Enchant to your Enchant Collection</h1><br/>
<p>Extract a Mystic Enchant from a Mystic Scroll to permanently add it to your Enchant Collection. This collection is realm wide!<br/><br/>
Saving enchants to your collection requires a Mystic Extract.<br/><br/>
Use an Enchanting Altar, click the Scrolls Tab, the click Save to Collection on the Mystic Enchant you want to permanently save.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\Mystic_Enchant_Collection_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Collect Mystic Enchants that empower your spells!</h1><br/>
<p>There is no limit to how many Extracts you can earn or Mystic Enchants you can collect!<br/><br/>
You can find Mystic Enchants that empower your current spells and archetype by reforging Mystic Scrolls or buying them from the Auction House.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\82_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Fly to the Crossroads at the Flightmaster!</h1><br/>
<p>The Flightpath to the Barrens is automatically unlocked! Visit the Flightmaster in your Capital City and fly to a new zone to continue leveling!<br/><br/>
The Crossroads is the most popular quest hub for Heroes leaving the capital for the first time.<br/><br/>
You can find nearby Flightmasters by using the Map Lens and selecting Flightmaster.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\82_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Unlock new Flightpaths at Flightmasters!</h1><br/>
<p>Interacting with a Flightmaster unlocks their Flightpath. Anytime you travel to a new zone, you should look for the Flightmaster’s green “!” in your faction's quest hub.<br/><br/>
Each Flightpath connects to other nearby locations. Unlocking multiple locations allows you to chain them together to fly even greater distances at once! Unlock the nodes between two locations to fly between those locations.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\97_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Earn Skill Card Packs from Silas!</h1><br/>
<p>Completing max level Scroll of Fortune quests at Silas grants Sealed Card Packs containing 5 random max-level Talent Skill Cards.<br/><br/>
Use Card Packs from your bags or Skill Cards Menu, then Card Packs and Cards tab.<br/><br/>
Skill Card Packs are found in almost all content. Your Skill Card Collection expands fast!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\97_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use Your Skill Card Pack to Reveal 5 Cards!</h1><br/>
<p>Each Skill Card Pack contains 5 random max-level Talent Skill Cards.<br/><br/>
Your revealed Skill Cards are automatically added to your Skill Card Collection.<br/><br/>
Your Skill Card Collection is shared across all characters on your account.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\97_3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Collect Max-Level Talent Cards!</h1><br/>
<p>Skill Card Packs grant max-level Talent Skill Cards directly.<br/><br/>
Open packs to expand your account-wide collection and give future builds more talent options.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\First_Class_Teleporter_1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Fast Travel to High-Level Zones and Capital Cities!</h1><br/>
<p>The First Class Experimental Teleporter allows you to air drop between Capital Cities and into high-level zones.<br/><br/>
This Teleporter is located in popular parts of the Capital Cities, it stands out and you won't miss it.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\First_Class_Teleporter_2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Steer your Parachute!</h1><br/>
<p>You will be dropped hundreds of yards into the air, don't worry, we provide a parachute that lasts just long enough to get you to the ground... safely!<br/><br/>
You can turn your camera to steer the direction of your parachute. Operator takes full responsibility for their steering!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\ilvlaqr:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reach Item Level 68 to Enter Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj!</h1><br/>
<p>Work towards an average item level of 68 to prepare for Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Gear Up with Call Board Caches and Manastorm!</h1><br/>
<p>Complete Call Board Daily Quests and run Manastorm to upgrade your gear.<br/><br/>
Call Board Caches provide gear up to the current raid tier based on your item level.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Advance Through Mythic+ Dungeons and Blackwing Lair!</h1><br/>
<p>Participate in Mythic+ Dungeons to obtain higher item level gear.<br/><br/>
Defeating bosses in Blackwing Lair or higher difficulties of previous raids also offers valuable upgrades.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\ilvlony:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reach Item Level 62 to Enter Onyxia's Lair!</h1><br/>
<p>Increase your average item level to 62 to prepare for Onyxia's Lair.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Use Call Board Caches and Manastorm!</h1><br/>
<p>Completing Call Board Daily Quests and running Manastorm are effective ways to upgrade your gear.<br/><br/>
Call Board Caches provide gear up to the current raid tier based on your item level.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\gearup3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Advance Through Mythic Dungeons and Molten Core!</h1><br/>
<p>Participate in Mythic Dungeons to obtain better gear.<br/><br/>
Defeating bosses in Molten Core or higher difficulties of previous raids also rewards higher item level equipment.<br/><br/>
Don't forget to try Mythic+ Dungeons for even greater rewards.</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerollingtalents1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reroll Talents!</h1><br/>
<p>|cffe6cc80|Hitem:97933|h[Scroll of Fortune: Talents]|h|r allows you to reroll Talents! Obtain them from Silas Darkmoon.<br/><br/>
Open Character Advancement, find a Talent you would like to reroll, and select Unlearn.<br/><br/>
You can always save your Scrolls of Fortune if you like all of your Talents!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerollingtalents2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Wildcard Tries to Find Synergy!</h1><br/>
<p>Wildcard isn't always 100% Random! Wildcard will often try to give you a Talents that synergizes with your Spells and vice versa.<br/><br/>
Save Talents you want to see synergy for, and reroll Talents you don't want to see synergy for. Wildcard will never stop trying to give you Synergies.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\rerollingtalents3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Talents Can Rank Up When Rerolling!</h1><br/>
<p>If you have Rank 1 of a Talent, you can upgrade it to higher ranks when Rerolling other talents! Talent Upgrade Rolls happen randomly.<br/><br/>
Make sure you hang on to lower ranks of talents! Rerolling other talents has a chance to upgrade any of your other talents.<br/><br/>
When you get a Talent Upgrade during a Reroll, you will still Roll into a new talent after receiving the upgraded.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\95_4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Reroll Strategically!</h1><br/>
<p>Focus on rerolling talents that do not directly increase your power or empower your core abilities you use the most!<br/><br/>
As you reroll your weakest or least relevant talents, your build will quickly fill up with talents that all add immense power.<br/><br/>
This method will ensure you get really strong, really fast! And maximize your Synergy Rolls!</p>

{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\zulgurub1:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Zul'Gurub is in Stranglethorn Vale!</h1><br/>
<p>The Zul'Gurub raid located in the north eastern part of Stranglethorn Vale.<br/><br/>
Flying to Booty Bay or using the First-Class Experimental Teleporter to air drop into Booty Bay is a quick way to travel to the raid!</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\zulgurub2:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Summon Your Raid at the Meeting Stone!</h1><br/>
<p>Use the Meeting Stone to help summon your raid, or accept a summon from other group members!<br/><br/>
The Zul'Gurub Meeting Stone is at the entrance of Zul'Gurub, directly East of Lake Nazferit and North of Mosh'Ogg Ogre Mound.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\zulgurub3:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Enter Zul'Gurub</h1><br/>
<p>Head east through the large open gate from the meeting stone.<br/><br/>
Proceed up the stone stairs, and run through the instance portal to enter Zul'Gurub.</p>
{page}
{T:Interface\Tutorials\PtA\zulgurub4:1024:406:1024:512:0:1024:59:465}
<h1 align="center">Defeat Hakkar in Zul'Gurub!</h1><br/>
<p>Hakkar is the final boss of Zul'Gurub.<br/><br/>
In order to defeat Hakkar, you should first defeat the priestesses spread throughout the instance. Each one left alive empowers Hakkar!<br/><br/>
Hakkar is located atop the central temple in the middle of the raid.</p>
